-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- SQUASHED BASELINE — 2026-07-30
--
-- The ONLY migration referenced by meta/_journal.json. Creates the complete
-- schema defined by packages/db/src/schema/ (95 tables, 38 enums) in one shot.
-- Generated by `pnpm --filter @repo/db db:generate` against a clean journal,
-- then this header + the guard below were prepended by hand. Nothing else in
-- the file was edited.
--
-- WHY THIS EXISTS
--   The journal had 13 entries against 58 .sql files: 45 migrations (78%) were
--   invisible to `drizzle-kit migrate`, and the only DDL for `images` /
--   `source_images` lived in an orphan directory referenced by nothing. A
--   from-zero rebuild produced a schema that did not match src/schema/. Rather
--   than reconstruct a 58-step history that was never replayed end-to-end, the
--   current schema is asserted directly.
--
-- WHEN IT RUNS
--   Its journal `when` is 1778726296694 — deliberately identical to the
--   original 0000_yummy_squadron_sinister. drizzle applies a migration only if
--   `last_applied.created_at < migration.folderMillis` (see drizzle-orm
--   pg-core/dialect.js `migrate()`), so on ANY database that already has a row
--   in drizzle.__drizzle_migrations this baseline is skipped. It runs only on
--   a virgin database. drizzle also wraps the whole run in one transaction, so
--   a mistake rolls back cleanly.
--
-- THE ONE REMAINING HAZARD
--   A database that is fully populated but whose drizzle.__drizzle_migrations
--   table is EMPTY (possible here: production migrations have been applied
--   out-of-band with psql since ~0013 — see docs/sessions/2026-07-29-DEPLOY-RUNBOOK.md).
--   The guard below turns that case into an immediate, readable abort instead
--   of a wall of "relation already exists".
--
--   To adopt this baseline on an existing, already-correct database:
--     INSERT INTO drizzle.__drizzle_migrations (hash, created_at)
--     VALUES (encode(digest(pg_read_file('<abs path to this file>'), 'sha256'), 'hex'),
--             1778726296694);
--   (or simply any row with created_at >= 1778726296694 — drizzle compares
--   timestamps, not hashes, when deciding what to apply).
--
-- THE 58 LEGACY .sql FILES ARE STILL HERE, unmodified, next to this one. They
-- are the historical record and the source of truth for what production had
-- applied; they are no longer referenced by the journal. See README.md in this
-- directory. To revert this re-baselining: move meta/_legacy-pre-2026-07-30/*
-- back up into meta/ and delete this file plus meta/0000_snapshot.json.
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

DO $guard$
BEGIN
  IF to_regclass('public.content_jobs') IS NOT NULL THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION
      'REFUSING TO APPLY 0000_baseline_2026_07_30: public.content_jobs already exists. '
      'This baseline is only for a virgin database. If this database is already correct, '
      'record it as applied in drizzle.__drizzle_migrations (see the header of this file) '
      'instead of running it.';
  END IF;
END
$guard$;
